# An end-of-day job that runs only on NYSE trading days (calendar `us/nyse`, calendars/us/nyse.calendar).
# On a weekend or an exchange holiday (Good Friday, Thanksgiving...) it does not run: with `|| Succeed` it
# succeeds at once without dispatching, so anything depending on it is not held up; without it, it would be
# `skipped` and its job page would say why, e.g. "not a working day: holiday Good Friday (us/nyse)".
# 21:30 UTC is after the 16:00 New York close all year round (20:00 UTC in summer, 21:00 in winter).
# Check a day with: borg admin calendar check us/nyse 20261126
Master: any
# Expect: succeeded
Command: echo "NYSE trading day $BORG_RUN_DATE: collecting closing prices"
Host: any
Calendar: us/nyse
Days: b || Succeed
StartAfter: 21:30
Timeout: 60
